course: dictionary
lesson: 9302
title: Specially and the extra care
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Specially» tells you that something was made, chosen or done for one particular purpose or person. «Anteaters get a specially made mushy mix» means the mix was made just for anteaters, not for any other animal.
explain: Look at the words next to «specially» to find its meaning. Specially made, specially designed, specially trained and specially for you all show that extra effort went into something. Check your idea by swapping in «for one particular purpose» and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In everyday talk, people sometimes use «specially» to mean «especially», which means particularly. In school writing, teachers often prefer «especially» for «particularly», so use «especially» in your own essays.
fact: «Specially» means for one particular purpose or person.
fact: «Specially» can also mean in a special or unusual way, done with extra care.
fact: Common phrases are specially for, specially made and specially trained.
fact: In everyday talk, «specially» can mean «especially», which means particularly.
fact: In school writing, teachers often prefer «especially» for «particularly».
exercise: «Anteaters get a specially made mushy mix that copies an ant diet.» What does specially show here? | It was made very quickly | It was made by accident | It tastes very sour | *It was made for one particular purpose
exercise: Which phrase shows something made for one particular person? | A cake that is very big | A cake eaten in the rain | A cake that was baked last year | *A cake specially made for your birthday
exercise: Mia says «specially» and «especially» mean the same in school writing. What is true? | Teachers always prefer «specially» for «particularly» | *Teachers often prefer «especially» for «particularly» | They never mean anything similar | «Specially» is always a noun
test: «Big earthquakes happen in particular parts of the world, and buildings in earthquake places are built specially.» What does specially mean? | Very high up | Badly and in a hurry | Under the ground | *With extra care for one particular purpose
test: Which phrase tells you a person was trained for one particular job? | Lost forever | *Specially trained | Very quickly | In the rain
exam: Which sentence uses specially to mean made for one particular person? | The dog ran specially fast | *Grandma knitted this scarf specially for you | The weather was specially cold today | We ate our lunch specially in the park
